{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that there would be no adverse impact on existing protected trees and landscaping features. The proposed hardstanding would also further diminish the greenery in the forecourt which would be harmful to the character and appearance of the building and the streetscene. The proposal would be contrary to Policies G7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DM22 and DM23 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed two storey front extension, together with the increase in roof height, creation of a crown roof and gabling of both roof flanks, would create an increase in bulk, width and height that would be overly dominant and out of keeping with to the character and appearance of the existing dwelling and the streetscene, appearing as a bulky incongruous feature in the locality that would have a detrimental effect on the visual appearance of the streetscene, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 (B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
